---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import {
  PopoverCalendar,
  PopoverHoverCards,
  PopoverPanels,
  PopoverPickers,
  PopoverPlacement,
  PopoverPlayground,
  PopoverQuickChat,
  PopoverSources,
  PopoverStatus,
} from "../../components/PopoverDemo";
---

<Docs
  title="Popover"
  description="Floating panels for details, pickers, filters, and quick chat."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Popover</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A floating panel tied to a button. Use it for source details, pickers,
    filters, and short forms. Unlike a menu it can hold any content, and unlike
    a dialog it leaves the rest of the page usable.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8" id="popover-demo"><PopoverPlayground client:load /></div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Popover usage"
      code={`import { Button } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/button";
import {
  Popover,
  PopoverContent,
  PopoverDescription,
  PopoverHeader,
  PopoverTitle,
  PopoverTrigger,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/popover";

<Popover>
  <PopoverTrigger render={<Button variant="outline" size="sm" />}>
    Sync status
  </PopoverTrigger>
  <PopoverContent align="end">
    <PopoverHeader>
      <PopoverTitle>Synced 2 minutes ago</PopoverTitle>
      <PopoverDescription>All 4 sources are up to date.</PopoverDescription>
    </PopoverHeader>
  </PopoverContent>
</Popover>`}
    />
    <p>
      Pass a <code>Button</code> to <code>PopoverTrigger</code> through <code
        >render</code
      >. Icon-only triggers need an <code>aria-label</code>. Add a <code
        >PopoverTitle</code
      > or an <code>aria-label</code> on the content so the panel has a name.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Sizes</h2>
    <p>
      <code>PopoverContent size</code> picks the width and padding. <code
        >"default"</code
      > is an 18rem padded panel for text. <code>"menu"</code> (24rem) and <code
        >"picker"</code
      > (18rem) have no padding so search lists can run edge to edge. <code
        >"panel"</code
      > fits filters and tabs up to 32rem. <code>"work-list"</code> is as wide as
      a panel and caps its height so a header, scroll area, and footer fit. <code
        >"app-actions"</code
      > is a 20rem scrolling card, and <code>"bud"</code> is a fixed-height quick
      chat window.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="popover-sources">
    <h2 class="section-title">Sources and help</h2>
    <p>
      Default-size popovers hold short explanations: a citation, why a
      repository is missing, or who can see a project. Load slow content in <code
        >onOpenChange</code
      > and show loading, error, and retry states inside the panel.
    </p>
    <PopoverSources client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Status</h2>
    <p>
      A toolbar status button can open with <code>defaultOpen</code> to call out a
      problem. Keep a visually hidden <code>role="status"</code> or <code
        >role="alert"</code
      > next to it so changes are announced even when the panel is closed.
    </p>
    <PopoverStatus client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Pickers</h2>
    <p>
      Pickers open above composers with <code>side="top"</code> and below toolbars
      by default. A picker trigger can also be a tooltip trigger. Show loading, failed,
      empty-search, and no-results states in the list, and clear the search when the
      picker closes.
    </p>
    <PopoverPickers client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Panels</h2>
    <p>
      The <code>panel</code> size holds tabs and filter forms. Control it with <code
        >open</code
      > and <code>onOpenChange</code> to keep it open while a rule is invalid, and
      close it after a valid rule is added.
    </p>
    <PopoverPanels client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Calendar</h2>
    <p>
      A date picker opens from the month title. The <code>work-list</code> size lists
      pending work and overlapping events, with a focusable scroll area and a footer
      link.
    </p>
    <PopoverCalendar client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Hover cards</h2>
    <p>
      <code>PopoverTrigger openOnHover</code> opens after <code>delay</code> and closes
      after <code>closeDelay</code>. Pass <code
        >{'initialFocus={(type) => type !== "mouse"}'}</code
      > so pointer hover doesn’t steal focus, while keyboard and touch users land
      inside.
    </p>
    <PopoverHoverCards client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Quick chat</h2>
    <p>
      A popover doesn’t need a trigger. Pass <code>anchor</code> to tie it to any
      element, <code>keepMounted</code> to keep its draft while closed, and <code
        >{"modal={false}"}</code
      > so the page stays usable. Cancel the outside press in <code
        >onOpenChange</code
      > when the launcher should toggle it, and return focus with <code
        >finalFocus</code
      >.
    </p>
    <PopoverQuickChat client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Placement</h2>
    <p>
      Set <code>side</code>, <code>align</code>, <code>sideOffset</code>, and <code
        >alignOffset</code
      >. Popovers open below and centered by default, and flip or shift to stay
      inside the viewport.
    </p>
    <PopoverPlacement client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="popover-api">
    <h2 class="section-title">API</h2>
    <p>
      <code>Popover</code> and <code>PopoverTrigger</code> wrap the Base UI popover
      root and trigger and take their props, including <code>modal</code>, <code
        >defaultOpen</code
      >, <code>openOnHover</code>, <code>delay</code>, <code>closeDelay</code>,
      and <code>render</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>PopoverContent</code> renders its own portal and positioner. It takes
      <code>size</code>, <code>side</code> (<code>"bottom"</code>), <code
        >align</code
      > (<code>"center"</code>), <code>sideOffset</code> (4), <code
        >alignOffset</code
      >, <code>collisionPadding</code> (8), <code>anchor</code>, <code
        >keepMounted</code
      >, <code>container</code>, and every Base UI popup prop such as <code
        >initialFocus</code
      > and <code>finalFocus</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>PopoverHeader</code> is a <code>div</code> that stacks <code
        >PopoverTitle</code
      > (an <code>h2</code>) and <code>PopoverDescription</code> (a <code
        >p</code
      >). Every part sets a <code>data-slot</code>, and you can override it.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The trigger has <code>aria-haspopup="dialog"</code> and <code
        >aria-expanded</code
      >. Enter and Space open the popover and move focus inside. Tab moves
      through its content, and Escape or an outside click closes it and returns
      focus to the trigger.
    </p>
    <p>
      Popovers fade and scale in from their side over 120ms; the app-actions and
      bud sizes take 180ms. Motion turns off when reduced motion is requested.
      In forced-colors mode the panel keeps a visible border.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Popovers use <code>--sprout-surface</code>, <code>--sprout-line</code>, <code
        >--sprout-text</code
      >, <code>--sprout-muted</code>, <code>--sprout-shadow-overlay</code>, and
      the panel radius. They need no brand color, so they look the same with the
      neutral and TulipFarm themes in light and dark mode.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
